    <string name="concatedral_nombre">Co-Cathedral of Saint María</string>
    <string name="concatedral_desc">
        The Co-Cathedral of Saint Mary is the spiritual heart of Cáceres\' old town.
        Its impressive Gothic architecture, side chapels filled with sacred art,
        and the legendary Black Christ make it a must-see visit.
    </string>

    <string name="baluarte_pozos_nombre">Baluarte de los Pozos</string>
    <string name="baluarte_pozos_desc">
        Located in one of the most photogenic areas of the Jewish quarter,
        this old fortress offers spectacular views of the lower city and the walls.
    </string>

    <string name="palacio_carvajal_nombre">Carvajal Palace</string>
    <string name="palacio_carvajal_desc">
        One of the most beautiful buildings in the historic center,
        featuring a Renaissance façade and a charming inner garden.
    </string>

    <string name="torre_bujaco_nombre">Bujaco Tower</string>
    <string name="torre_bujaco_desc">
        The true symbol of Cáceres, this 12th-century Almohad tower dominates the Main Square
        and offers stunning panoramic views.
    </string>

    <string name="torre_ciguenas_nombre">Palace and Tower of the Storks</string>
    <string name="torre_ciguenas_desc">
        A unique palace whose tower was never dismantled, preserving its medieval height
        and crowned by storks, symbols of the city.
    </string>

    <string name="plaza_mayor_nombre">Main Square</string>
    <string name="plaza_mayor_desc">
        Lively and spacious, the Main Square is the gateway to the monumental city
        and the perfect starting point for any visit.
    </string>

    <string name="arco_estrella_nombre">Star Arch</string>
    <string name="arco_estrella_desc">
        This Baroque arch is the most iconic entrance to the old town,
        connecting modern life with medieval streets.
    </string>

    <string name="casco_historico_nombre">Historic Old Town</string>
    <string name="casco_historico_desc">
        A UNESCO World Heritage Site, Cáceres\' old town is one of the best preserved in Europe,
        filled with palaces, towers, and timeless streets.
    </string>
